cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ChemMaster: A local-first computational chemistry agent with LLM tool use"
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sophie
    family-names: Zhang
    email: fhoueff41082@outlook.com
    affiliation: "ChemMaster contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/your-username/chemaster"
url: "https://github.com/your-username/chemaster"
abstract: >-
  ChemMaster is a Claude-Code-style local agent for computational
  chemistry. Users issue calculation tasks in natural language; a real
  LLM (Anthropic Claude, MiniMax M2.7, Qwen, DeepSeek, or local
  vLLM/llama.cpp via the OpenAI-compatible interface) drives a
  registry of MCP tools (psi4, xTB, ORCA, BDF, MultiWFN, cclib,
  RDKit/ASE, SLURM-over-SSH) to plan, execute, monitor, and report
  back. Designed for transparent, reproducible workflows: every step
  of the agent loop is persisted as a JSON trajectory, and a
  paper-ready Markdown report is auto-generated.
keywords:
  - computational-chemistry
  - large-language-models
  - tool-use
  - tadf
  - dft
  - tddft
  - psi4
  - orca
  - bdf
  - mcp
  - claude-code
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0a1
date-released: "2026-04-30"
